# Super Roc @VERSION@ for Linux x86_64

Build @REVISION@ of Super Roc for AMD Strix Halo (gfx1151).

## Requirements

- An AMD Ryzen AI Max (Strix Halo, gfx1151) system.
- Ubuntu 24.04 or a compatible distribution.
- ROCm 7.2: the HIP runtime, hipBLAS, rocBLAS and hipBLASLt. With AMD's ROCm
  package repository configured: `sudo apt install hip-runtime-amd hipblas rocblas hipblaslt`.
- These system libraries:
  `sudo apt install libcurl4t64 libicu74 libpng16-16t64 libjpeg-turbo8 libwebp7 libssl3t64 libgomp1 zlib1g`.

## Install

```bash
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
tar -xzf @NAME@.tar.gz
```

The archive runs where it is unpacked:

```bash
./@NAME@/bin/superroc --version
```

To install it system-wide:

```bash
sudo cp -r @NAME@/bin @NAME@/share /usr/local/
```

The binary looks for the ROCm libraries in `/opt/rocm/lib`. If ROCm is
installed elsewhere, add its library directory before running:
`export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/path/to/rocm/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH`.

## Run

```bash
superroc serve -i 127.0.0.1 -p 8080 llm -m /path/to/model.gguf --context 32768
```

The server speaks the OpenAI and Anthropic APIs on the chosen port. See the
project documentation for the supported models and every option.

